{"id":"mahabharata-12-017","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":17,"title":"सप्तदशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 17 · Yudhishthira on desire and attachment","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira answers that restlessness, pride and greed are the causes of sorrow, and compares the greedy man to a tiger that kills much for one belly. He says that release comes to the man who gives up both the fruits of action and the bond of desire.","kn":"ಚಂಚಲತೆ, ಗರ್ವ, ಲೋಭವೇ ದುಃಖದ ಕಾರಣವೆಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಉತ್ತರಿಸಿ ಲೋಭಿಯನ್ನು ಒಂದು ಹೊಟ್ಟೆಗಾಗಿ ಬಹಳ ಕೊಲ್ಲುವ ಹುಲಿಗೆ ಹೋಲಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಕರ್ಮಫಲ, ಆಸೆಯ ಬಂಧನ ಎರಡನ್ನೂ ತೊರೆದವನಿಗೆ ಮೋಕ್ಷ ಸಿಗುತ್ತದೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर उत्तर देते हैं कि चंचलता, अभिमान और लोभ दुःख के कारण हैं, और लोभी की तुलना उस बाघ से करते हैं जो एक पेट के लिए बहुत मारता है। वे कहते हैं कि कर्मफल और इच्छा का बन्धन दोनों छोड़ने वाले को मुक्ति मिलती है।","te":"చంచలత్వం, గర్వం, లోభం దుఃఖానికి కారణాలని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు బదులిచ్చి లోభిని ఒక్క కడుపు కోసం ఎంతో చంపే పులితో పోలుస్తాడు. కర్మఫలాన్ని, కోరిక బంధాన్ని రెంటినీ వదిలినవానికి మోక్షం లభిస్తుందంటాడు.","ta":"அலைபாய்தல், செருக்கு, பேராசை துயருக்குக் காரணங்கள் என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் பதிலளித்துப் பேராசைக்காரனை ஒரே வயிற்றுக்காகப் பலரைக் கொல்லும் புலியுடன் ஒப்பிடுகிறார். செயலின் பலனையும் ஆசையின் பிணைப்பையும் துறப்பவனுக்கு விடுதலை என்கிறார்.","ml":"അസ്വസ്ഥത, അഹങ്കാരം, അത്യാഗ്രഹം എന്നിവയാണ് ദുഃഖത്തിന്റെ കാരണമെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ മറുപടി പറയുന്നു; ഒരു വയറിനുവേണ്ടി ഒരുപാടു പേരെ കൊല്ലുന്ന കടുവയോടാണ് അത്യാഗ്രഹിയെ അദ്ദേഹം ഉപമിക്കുന്നത്. കർമ്മഫലത്തെയും ആഗ്രഹത്തിന്റെ ബന്ധനത്തെയും ഒരുപോലെ ഉപേക്ഷിക്കുന്നവനാണ് മോചനം നേടുന്നതെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.17; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"राजधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Rajadharma Parva (Duties of kings)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"असंतोषः प्रमादश्च मदो रागोऽप्रशान्तता ।\nबलं मोहोऽभिमानश्च उद्वेगश्चापि सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Discontent, negligence, pride, passion, restlessness, force, delusion, conceit and agitation in every way:"}},{"n":2,"text":"एभिः पाप्मभिराविष्टो राज्यं त्वमभिकाङ्क्षसि ।\nनिरामिषो विनिर्मुक्तः प्रशान्तः सुसुखी भव ॥","meaning":{"en":"possessed by these sins, you long for the kingdom. Be free of flesh (desire), released, calm and very happy."}},{"n":3,"text":"य इमामखिलां भूमिं शिष्यादेको महीपतिः ।\nतस्याप्युदरमेवैकं किमिदं त्वं प्रशंससि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even the one king who might rule this entire earth has only one belly. Why do you praise this?"}},{"n":4,"text":"नाह्ना पूरयितुं शक्या न मासेन नरर्षभ ।\nअपूर्यां पूरयन्निच्छामायुषापि न शक्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It cannot be filled in a day or a month, bull among men; trying to fill the unfillable, one could not do it in a whole lifetime."}},{"n":5,"text":"यथेद्धः प्रज्वलत्यग्निरसमिद्धः प्रशाम्यति ।\nअल्पाहारतया त्वग्निं शमयौदर्यमुत्थितम् ।\nजयोदरं पृथिव्या ते श्रेयो निर्जितया जितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As fire when fed blazes and when unfed goes out, so calm the belly-fire that has risen by eating little. Conquer the belly; for you, to conquer the earth is a lesser good than being conquered itself."}},{"n":6,"text":"मानुषान्कामभोगांस्त्वमैश्वर्यं च प्रशंससि ।\nअभोगिनोऽबलाश्चैव यान्ति स्थानमनुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You praise human pleasures and sovereignty, but those who enjoy nothing and have no strength reach the highest state."}},{"n":7,"text":"योगक्षेमौ च राष्ट्रस्य धर्माधर्मौ त्वयि स्थितौ ।\nमुच्यस्व महतो भारात्त्यागमेवाभिसंश्रय ॥","meaning":{"en":"The security and welfare of a kingdom, dharma and adharma, rest on you. Free yourself of this great burden; take refuge in renunciation alone."}},{"n":8,"text":"एकोदरकृते व्याघ्रः करोति विघसं बहु ।\nतमन्येऽप्युपजीवन्ति मन्दवेगंचरा मृगाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A tiger makes many a kill for the sake of one belly, and other creatures with slow movements live on it."}},{"n":9,"text":"विषयान्प्रतिसंहृत्य संन्यासं कुरुते यतिः ।\nन च तुष्यन्ति राजानः पश्य बुद्ध्यन्तरं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"A seeker withdraws from the objects of the senses and takes up renunciation, while kings are never satisfied. See how far apart the minds are."}},{"n":10,"text":"पत्राहारैरश्मकुट्टैर्दन्तोलूखलिकैस्तथा ।\nअब्भक्षैर्वायुभक्षैश्च तैरयं नरको जितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hermits who eat leaves, who crush grain with stones, who use their teeth as mortars, who live on water or on air: by them this hell has been conquered."}},{"n":11,"text":"यश्चेमां वसुधां कृत्स्नां प्रशासेदखिलां नृपः ।\nतुल्याश्मकाञ्चनो यश्च स कृतार्थो न पार्थिवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king who rules this entire earth and a man who sees a stone and gold as equal: the latter has accomplished his aim; the king has not."}},{"n":12,"text":"संकल्पेषु निरारम्भो निराशो निर्ममो भव ।\nविशोकं स्थानमातिष्ठ इह चामुत्र चाव्ययम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Be free of undertaking in your resolves, free of hope and possessiveness. Stand in the place without sorrow, which is imperishable here and hereafter."}},{"n":13,"text":"निरामिषा न शोचन्ति शोचसि त्वं किमामिषम् ।\nपरित्यज्यामिषं सर्वं मृषावादात्प्रमोक्ष्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those without flesh do not grieve. Why do you grieve for flesh? Giving up all flesh, you will be freed from false speech."}},{"n":14,"text":"पन्थानौ पितृयानश्च देवयानश्च विश्रुतौ ।\nईजानाः पितृयानेन देवयानेन मोक्षिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two paths are well known: the way of the ancestors and the way of the gods. Those who sacrifice go by the ancestors' way, and the seekers of release by the way of the gods."}},{"n":15,"text":"तपसा ब्रह्मचर्येण स्वाध्यायेन च पाविताः ।\nविमुच्य देहान्वै भान्ति मृत्योरविषयं गताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Purified by austerity, celibacy and study, they cast off their bodies and shine, having gone beyond the reach of death."}},{"n":16,"text":"आमिषं बन्धनं लोके कर्मेहोक्तं तथामिषम् ।\nताभ्यां विमुक्तः पाशाभ्यां पदमाप्नोति तत्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this world, \"flesh\" is bondage, and action is also called flesh. Freed from those two snares, one reaches the highest state."}},{"n":17,"text":"अपि गाथामिमां गीतां जनकेन वदन्त्युत ।\nनिर्द्वंद्वेन विमुक्तेन मोक्षं समनुपश्यता ॥","meaning":{"en":"They also tell this verse, sung by Janaka, free from the pairs of opposites and liberated, who saw release."}},{"n":18,"text":"अनन्तं बत मे वित्तं यस्य मे नास्ति किंचन ।\nमिथिलायां प्रदीप्तायां न मे दह्यति किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Endless indeed is my wealth, though I own nothing. When Mithila burns, nothing of mine is burned.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"प्रज्ञाप्रासादमारुह्य नशोच्याञ्शोचतो जनान् ।\nजगतीस्थानिवाद्रिस्थो मन्दबुद्धीनवेक्षते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Climbing the palace of wisdom, a man looks down on the grieving people who need not be mourned, as one on a mountain looks at those on the ground, dull in mind."}},{"n":20,"text":"दृश्यं पश्यति यः पश्यन्स चक्षुष्मान्स बुद्धिमान् ।\nअज्ञातानां च विज्ञानात्संबोधाद्बुद्धिरुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who sees what can be seen is the one with eyes and the wise one. From knowing what was unknown, through awakening, one is called wise."}},{"n":21,"text":"यस्तु वाचं विजानाति बहुमानमियात्स वै ।\nब्रह्मभावप्रसूतानां वैद्यानां भावितात्मनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who truly understands speech deserves great honor, among knowers of the Veda, born of the state of Brahman and of cultivated self."}},{"n":22,"text":"यदा भूतपृथग्भावमेकस्थमनुपश्यति ।\nतत एव च विस्तारं ब्रह्म संपद्यते तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"When one sees the separate natures of beings as resting in one, and from that very one their spreading out, then one attains Brahman."}},{"n":23,"text":"ते जनास्तां गतिं यान्ति नाविद्वांसोऽल्पचेतसः ।\nनाबुद्धयो नातपसः सर्वं बुद्धौ प्रतिष्ठितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who reach that goal are not the unlearned and small-minded, nor the unwise, nor those without austerity. Everything rests on understanding."}}]}]}